{% set services = notice.services|join(', ') %}
{% if notice.code == 'action_sent' and refusals %}
    {% for refusal in refusals %}
    <p class="notice toast drift" role="alert" data-notice-error data-service-refusal="{{ refusal.scope }}">The {{ notice.parameters.action }} was refused by {{ refusal.scope }}: {{ refusal.message }}</p>
    {% endfor %}
{% elseif notice.code == 'action_sent' %}
    <p class="notice toast" role="status" data-notice>Action sent: {{ notice.parameters.action }} to {{ services }}{% if notice.parameters.failure is defined %} for the failure {{ notice.parameters.failure }}{% endif %}{% if notice.parameters.affected is defined %}: {{ notice.parameters.action == 'replay' ? 'replayed' : 'deleted' }} <span data-affected>{{ notice.parameters.affected }}</span> {{ notice.parameters.affected == '1' ? 'dead letter' : 'dead letters' }}{% endif %}. The service answered with a fresh snapshot, and Pulse asks for one more a few seconds later. If the service refuses the action, it shows as unreachable after the reply timeout.</p>
{% else %}
    <p class="notice toast drift" role="alert" data-notice-error>
    {% if notice.code == 'send_failed' %}The action could not be sent to {{ services }}; the service shows the reason.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'nothing_selected' %}No dead letters were selected. Tick at least one dead letter, or use the filter actions.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'no_filter_condition' %}A filter action needs at least one filter condition (message name, exception class, failure, failed from or failed to), as without one it would apply to every dead letter. Fill one in, or select dead letters by id instead.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'search_not_stored' %}A search narrows only the list Pulse shows, so an action on a filter cannot honour it and would reach more dead letters than you see. Clear the search to act on the filter, or tick the dead letters you found and act on the selection.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'unknown_service' %}That service is not configured in PULSE_SERVICES, so Pulse cannot send it dead letter actions. Pick one of the listed services.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'not_configured' %}Service "{{ notice.parameters.service }}" has dead letter not configured in its latest snapshot, so Pulse sends it no dead letter actions. Enable it with DbalConfiguration::createWithDefaults()->withDeadLetter(true) in that service, then refresh.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'no_dead_letters_anywhere' %}No service has dead letter configured, so there is nothing to act on.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'unknown_channel' %}Service "{{ notice.parameters.service }}" does not register a channel "{{ notice.parameters.channel }}" in its latest snapshot, so nothing was replayed. Pick one of its channels from the list, or leave it empty to replay to the original channel; refresh if the channel was added recently.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'target_needs_service' %}A replay target channel belongs to one service. Choose a single service in the filter to replay to a channel, or leave the channel empty to replay to each original channel.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'target_per_service' %}The replay channel is picked per service, in the select inside that service's own section. Pick it there, or leave it empty to replay to the original channel.
    {% elseif notice.code == 'invalid_date' %}"{{ notice.parameters.field == 'failedFrom' ? 'Failed from' : 'Failed to' }}" is not a valid UTC date and time. Enter it as 2026-10-20T12:00:00, or clear it.
    {% endif %}
    </p>
{% endif %}
